      "notes": "Fischer et al. report a thermal EOS for iron-saturated FeO, not a standalone 300 K BM3. The Fe0.94O starting powder was mixed with Fe and the authors treat the equilibrated high-P-T oxide as approximately stoichiometric FeO. Reported sample temperatures already include the source's 3% downward axial-gradient correction and must be evaluated at their tabulated values. The current-study supplement contributes 21 numerical B8 volumes; one-peak detections have no volume and are excluded, while Figure 3 assigns +/-0.1 cm^3/mol plotting errors when two-peak uncertainties could not be constrained. Ozawa's printed Table 2 contributes 8 B8 P-V-T rows and is bundled at printed precision. Fischer's exact combined row selection and regression weights/objective are not printed. The source explicitly warns against extrapolating this EOS far beyond the B8 data range.",
