      "notes": "The dataset preserves the official workbook's full numeric precision, normalized to 12 significant digits. Asterisks are represented by b8_observation=detected_one_peak_no_volume; dagger marks are represented by b1_observation=rhombohedrally_distorted_detected_no_volume; double-dagger rows retain the measured B8 values and their blank raw uncertainty. The separate B8 fit-uncertainty column copies every constrained workbook value and assigns 0.1 cm^3/mol only to the three double-dagger volumes, following the Figure 3 caption; it remains blank when no volume was measured. The supplement labels numeric error columns generically with +/- and does not define a statistic. Temperatures are the reported values after the paper's 3% axial-gradient correction, not values reduced to 300 K.",
